 card=('The principle', 'every alternative would be an unexplained choice or would not last', 'By the principle of sufficient reason (the principle at the root of Hockney\'s God Series), a method that beats the meetings must have a reason. The reasons available to algorithms are laws. 3-SAT has none.'),
 left=('Easy cases', 'Every fast method we can describe has its reason: a law it follows.'),
 right=('Hard cases', 'Where no law exists, the puzzle looks balanced from every side, and there is nothing to follow.'),
